{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nw \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & y \\ar[d] \\\\\nx \\ar[r] & z }\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$w \\to y \\to z$", "MATH_0005": "$w \\to x \\to z$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:996a4684fed53d3a51dc4ccdee337a47aef96b962ac152189110fc98b1f21f1c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa8390bac597f4278a39276f785a79e78d0a73ea5fd63331dcd0b6873935b202", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we introduce <MATH_0001>-fibre products. Suppose that <MATH_0002>\nis a 2-category. We say that a diagram\n<MATH_0003>\n2-commutes if the two 1-morphisms <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are\n2-isomorphic. In a 2-category it is more natural to ask for 2-commutativity\nof diagrams than for actually commuting diagrams. (Indeed, some may say that\nwe should not work with strict 2-categories at all, and in a ``weak''\n2-category the notion of a commutative diagram of 1-morphisms does not even\nmake sense.) Correspondingly the notion of a fibre product has to be adjusted.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a112d3e01062d37541336926395e78b9c6cd2499e763e78e4c83bbb07c19e8cf", "unit_id": "tag:003O:p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTE_0001": "\\footnote{In fact it seems in the $2$-category case\nthat one could define another 2-category of 2-commutative diagrams where\nthe direction of the arrows $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ is reversed, or even\nwhere the direction of only one of them is reversed. This is why\nwe restrict to $(2, 1)$-categories later on.}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$x, y, z\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$f\\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(x, z)$", "MATH_0005": "$g\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(y, z)$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$g$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& w \\ar[r]_a \\ar[d]_b & x \\ar[d]^{f} \\\\\n& y \\ar[r]^{g} & z. }\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$2$", "MATH_0010": "$2$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$g$", "MATH_0013": "$2$", "MATH_0014": "$(w, a, b, \\phi)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0016": "$\\phi : f \\circ a \\to g \\circ b$", "MATH_0017": "$(w', a', b', \\phi')$", "MATH_0018": "$(w, a, b, \\phi)$", "MATH_0019": "$(k : w' \\to w, \\alpha : a' \\to a \\circ k, \\beta : b' \\to b \\circ k)$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nf \\circ a'\n\\ar[rr]_{\\text{id}_f \\star \\alpha}\n\\ar[d]_{\\phi'}\n& &\nf \\circ a \\circ k\n\\ar[d]^{\\phi \\star \\text{id}_k}\n\\\\\ng \\circ b'\n\\ar[rr]^{\\text{id}_g \\star \\beta}\n& &\ng \\circ b \\circ k\n}\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$1$", "MATH_0022": "$(k', \\alpha', \\beta') : (w'', a'', b'', \\phi'') \\to\n(w', \\alpha', \\beta', \\phi')$", "MATH_0023": "$1$", "MATH_0024": "$$\n(k, \\alpha, \\beta) \\circ (k', \\alpha', \\beta') =\n(k \\circ k',\n(\\alpha \\star \\text{id}_{k'}) \\circ \\alpha',\n(\\beta \\star \\text{id}_{k'}) \\circ \\beta'),\n$$", "MATH_0025": "$1$", "MATH_0026": "$(k_i, \\alpha_i, \\beta_i)$", "MATH_0027": "$i = 1, 2$", "MATH_0028": "$\\delta : k_1 \\to k_2$", "MATH_0029": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\na'\n\\ar[rd]_{\\alpha_2}\n\\ar[r]_{\\alpha_1} &\na \\circ k_1\n\\ar[d]^{\\text{id}_a \\star \\delta} &\n&\nb \\circ k_1\n\\ar[d]_{\\text{id}_b \\star \\delta} &\nb'\n\\ar[l]^{\\beta_1}\n\\ar[ld]^{\\beta_2}\n\\\\\n&\na \\circ k_2\n&\n&\nb \\circ k_2\n&\n}\n$$", "MATH_0030": "$2$", "MATH_0031": "$\\delta$", "MATH_0032": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0033": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(w'', a'', b'', \\phi'')\n\\rrtwocell^{(k'_1, \\alpha'_1, \\beta'_1)}_{(k'_2, \\alpha'_2, \\beta'_2)}{\\delta'}\n& &\n(w', a', b', \\phi')\n\\rrtwocell^{(k_1, \\alpha_1, \\beta_1)}_{(k_2, \\alpha_2, \\beta_2)}{\\delta}\n& &\n(w, a, b, \\phi)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0034": "$$\n\\xymatrix@C=12pc{\n(w'', a'', b'', \\phi'')\n\\rtwocell^{(k_1 \\circ k'_1, (\\alpha_1 \\star \\text{id}_{k'_1}) \\circ \\alpha'_1, (\\beta_1 \\star \\text{id}_{k'_1}) \\circ \\beta'_1)}_{(k_2 \\circ k'_2, (\\alpha_2 \\star \\text{id}_{k'_2}) \\circ \\alpha'_2, (\\beta_2 \\star \\text{id}_{k'_2}) \\circ \\beta'_2)}{\\ \\ \\ \\delta \\star \\delta'}\n&\n(w, a, b, \\phi)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0035": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0036": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0037": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0038": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0039": "$2$", "MATH_0040": "$2$", "MATH_0041": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0042": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0043": "$(2, 1)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\item", "STRUCT_0010": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d952940534c0687a3c3b4b67eb726829ef0cb445084e1f37927017cdd0986f2a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c6462a5e0d30a2ddc6d0d1b2070b2c27e8f2784b931c1aea3b94e4bbd3289163", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a <MATH_0002>-category. Let <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>.\nIn order to define the 2-fibre product of <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007> we are going to look at\n2-commutative diagrams\n<MATH_0008>\nNow in the case of categories, the fibre product is a final object in the\ncategory of such diagrams. Correspondingly a 2-fibre product is a final object\nin a 2-category (see definition below). The <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0009>-category\nof <MATH_0010>-commutative diagrams over <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the <MATH_0013>-category defined as follows:\n<STRUCT_0003>\n<STRUCT_0004> Objects are quadruples <MATH_0014> as above where <MATH_0015>\nis an invertible 2-morphism <MATH_0016>,\n<STRUCT_0005> 1-morphisms from <MATH_0017> to <MATH_0018> are given by\n<MATH_0019>\nsuch that\n<MATH_0020>\nis commutative,\n<STRUCT_0006> given a second <MATH_0021>-morphism\n<MATH_0022> the composition of <MATH_0023>-morphisms\nis given by the rule\n<MATH_0024>\n<STRUCT_0007> a 2-morphism between <MATH_0025>-morphisms\n<MATH_0026>, <MATH_0027> with the same source and target\nis given by a 2-morphism <MATH_0028> such that\n<MATH_0029>\ncommute,\n<STRUCT_0008> vertical composition of <MATH_0030>-morphisms is given by\nvertical composition of the morphisms <MATH_0031> in <MATH_0032>, and\n<STRUCT_0009> horizontal composition of the diagram\n<MATH_0033>\nis given by the diagram\n<MATH_0034>\n<STRUCT_0010>\nNote that if <MATH_0035> is actually a <MATH_0036>-category,\nthe morphisms <MATH_0037> and <MATH_0038> in (2) above are automatically\nalso isomorphisms<FOOTNOTE_0001>.\nIn addition the <MATH_0039>-category of\n<MATH_0040>-commutative diagrams is also a <MATH_0041>-category if <MATH_0042> is\na <MATH_0043>-category.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:01518a62a6017138a01f70500567b5c2932fba036459ab715ca51c922516c8f3", "unit_id": "tag:003O:p002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "MATH_0004": "$y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$y \\to x$", "MATH_0006": "$y \\to x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-final-object-2-category}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:59efab1c1ea0ccb978c9aa0b701dd3136772ca03944295bb1ba0e084eb6d5e8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10c7dc7adc3db8584d85f1794015c019d0f17874e7820250d51a4635169c05a7", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>final object<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of a <MATH_0001>-category\n<MATH_0002> is an object <MATH_0003> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for every <MATH_0004> there is a morphism <MATH_0005>,\nand\n<STRUCT_0003> every two morphisms <MATH_0006> are isomorphic by a unique 2-morphism.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1598fb0fa88cf70df6df28a6c32414c9a9a328315cbd62b5c6232336c8dde693", "unit_id": "tag:003O:definition"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$(2, 1)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:58d77599d938213bf05e5d987243c7888364dd477890adeb33abb5acb5338d3e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:588583807a84050173272a80f6ad22ae719aea664673d4d77fd84759bc2c177b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLikely, in the more general case of <MATH_0001>-categories there are different\nflavours of final objects. We do not want to get into this and hence\nwe only define <MATH_0002>-fibre products in the <MATH_0003>-case.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3a3fa7a636220ce8a39eb5b5fd718af0d9e43e6b24c70fd023b63af776fd61f3", "unit_id": "tag:003O:p003"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$(2, 1)$", "MATH_0003": "$x, y, z\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$f\\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(x, z)$", "MATH_0005": "$g\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(y, z)$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$g$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\times_z y\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0009": "$p\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times_z y, x)$", "MATH_0010": "$q\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times_z y, y)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n& x \\times_z y \\ar[r]^{p} \\ar[d]_q & x \\ar[d]^{f} \\\\\n& y \\ar[r]^{g} & z }\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\psi : f \\circ p \\to g \\circ q$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-2-fibre-products}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{definition}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:930156984d3d25c2bc67aa3744c2829f072013b8c45f5bd55e3564925e39c2fb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2df7c610f564e0e363873da7432490ccc0097e6c1ca4c82d79a6893d3f6d7528", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a <MATH_0002>-category.\nLet <MATH_0003> and\n<MATH_0004>\nand <MATH_0005>. A\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>2-fibre product of <MATH_0006> and <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is\na final object in the category of 2-commutative diagrams\ndescribed above. If a 2-fibre product exists we\nwill denote it <MATH_0008>, and denote the\nrequired morphisms <MATH_0009> and\n<MATH_0010> making the diagram\n<MATH_0011>\n2-commute and we will denote the given invertible\n2-morphism exhibiting this by <MATH_0012>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cfb0538eb5eea38b3d9841f1c920ff83eaf6d9e85814d79cb4b21ae914553484", "unit_id": "tag:003O:definition-002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$w\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$a \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x)$", "MATH_0003": "$b \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(w, y)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\phi : f \\circ a \\to g\\circ b$", "MATH_0005": "$\\gamma \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x \\times_z y)$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nw\\ar[rrrd]^a \\ar@{-->}[rrd]_\\gamma \\ar[rrdd]_b & & \\\\\n& & x \\times_z y \\ar[r]_p \\ar[d]_q & x \\ar[d]^{f} \\\\\n& & y \\ar[r]^{g} & z }\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$a \\to p \\circ \\gamma$", "MATH_0008": "$b \\to q \\circ \\gamma$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nf \\circ a \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_\\phi &\nf \\circ p \\circ \\gamma\n\\ar[d]^{\\psi \\star \\text{id}_\\gamma}\n\\\\\ng\\circ b\n\\ar[r]\n&\ng \\circ q \\circ \\gamma\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\gamma$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5893bd80b26f74dd9da9693b0bb9a8aaad413b466c4a2f365931bb37a194f563", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d1e89ae81768c4b0cf06c3c1a1a7ca071a56e53d7d0dcd9e7bbdd9b1ad064dd", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThus the following universal property holds: for any\n<MATH_0001> and morphisms\n<MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> with a given 2-isomorphism\n<MATH_0004>\nthere is a <MATH_0005>\nmaking the diagram\n<MATH_0006>\n2-commute such that for suitable choices of\n<MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008>\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0009>\ncommutes. Moreover <MATH_0010> is unique up to isomorphism.\nOf course the exact properties are finer than this. All of the\ncases of 2-fibre products that we will need later on come from the following\nexample of 2-fibre products in the 2-category of categories.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6416c2f6c88f78c4b11567d342fce8d4ca59cd8df3ef1af2b4e9d2fe10366bd5", "unit_id": "tag:003O:p004"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$G : \\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A} \\times_\\mathcal{C} \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A} \\times_\\mathcal{C} \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0008": "$(A, B, f)$", "MATH_0009": "$A\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0010": "$B\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{B})$", "MATH_0011": "$f : F(A) \\to G(B)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0013": "$(A, B, f) \\to (A', B', f')$", "MATH_0014": "$(a, b)$", "MATH_0015": "$a : A \\to A'$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0017": "$b : B \\to B'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nF(A) \\ar[r]^f \\ar[d]^{F(a)} & G(B) \\ar[d]^{G(b)} \\\\\nF(A') \\ar[r]^{f'} & G(B')\n}\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$p : \\mathcal{A} \\times_\\mathcal{C}\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0021": "$q : \\mathcal{A} \\times_\\mathcal{C}\\mathcal{B} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0022": "$$\np(A, B, f) = A, \\quad q(A, B, f) = B,\n$$", "MATH_0023": "$\\psi : F \\circ p \\to G \\circ q$", "MATH_0024": "$\\xi = (A, B, f)$", "MATH_0025": "$\\psi_\\xi = f : F(p(\\xi)) = F(A) \\to G(B) = G(q(\\xi))$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-2-fibre-product-categories}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{example}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:48514a165a100903e00388e8bc3c900bb058e197e93d0d825e9b16582f31193c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d98dfe66bf2cd2f1ab430ee6cbda5be668cddd33bb8284c41d1210d41b1ffc07", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>, and <MATH_0003> be categories.\nLet <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005