{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b15315ec3c2fa7b154c0d17c24b63d47f12b572ea3fa602a460510e1a685b882", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5a090ab2629296262ebed12678128677a6e227b28f80953216286ad5fb31a3a", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe claim that this means you can work with these <MATH_0001>-fibre products\njust like with ordinary fibre products. Here are some further lemmas\nthat actually come up later.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:52de8d3eb6a86f97112f6d02c7868f678645b19f778e2b8657d0c8bb960837b9", "unit_id": "tag:003O:p006"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{C}_3 \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & \\mathcal{S} \\ar[d]^\\Delta \\\\\n\\mathcal{C}_1 \\times \\mathcal{C}_2 \\ar[r]^{G_1 \\times G_2} &\n\\mathcal{S} \\times \\mathcal{S}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}_3 \\cong\n\\mathcal{C}_1 \\times_{G_1, \\mathcal{S}, G_2} \\mathcal{C}_2$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-1}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30e31d088c4ffecb4dd1ecf1392dd51b890f3f77571647abcc0998110cb4cef7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a5bc7e113a54bfa2d39602b19e909d23941ebd042a1e3b4c5fce50d6f2bdd5f", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a <MATH_0002>-fibre product of categories.\nThen there is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8f5007c0e3b624214286324f63521b2e47183de8b143ec6ce2973478b1f7d47a", "unit_id": "tag:003O:lemma-007"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_3$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\mathcal{C}_1 \\times \\mathcal{C}_2)\\times_{\\mathcal{S} \\times \\mathcal{S}}\n\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$((X_1, X_2), S, \\phi)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\phi = (\\phi_1, \\phi_2) : (G_1(X_1), G_2(X_2)) \\to (S, S)$", "MATH_0005": "$(X_1, X_2, \\phi_2^{-1} \\circ \\phi_1)$", "MATH_0006": "$(X_1, X_2, \\psi)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}_1 \\times_{G_1, \\mathcal{S}, G_2} \\mathcal{C}_2$", "MATH_0008": "$((X_1, X_2), G_2(X_2), (\\psi, \\text{id}_{G_2(X_2)}))$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-2-fibre-product-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fab70eb0efcb905286d8071c825bbecc83508d7511947da938e7a9d37981db35", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9592a3bb934f0622f91b80fa8c5d0f0c0744d5506184b88e48615a0b43d54285", "source_text": "We may assume that <MATH_0001> is the category\n<MATH_0002> constructed in Example <REF_0001>.\nHence an object is a triple\n<MATH_0003> where\n<MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism. Thus we can associate to this the triple\n<MATH_0005>.\nConversely, if <MATH_0006> is an object of\n<MATH_0007>,\nthen we can associate to this the triple\n<MATH_0008>.\nWe claim these constructions given mutually inverse functors.\nWe omit describing how to deal with morphisms\nand showing they are mutually inverse.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e4969845e3534816ea59c99fc16e18a77cd8d5e8d52027be53bdc46ab7c9326", "unit_id": "tag:003O:proof-p007"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "003O", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{C}' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & \\mathcal{S} \\ar[d]^\\Delta \\\\\n\\mathcal{C} \\ar[r]^{(G_1, G_2)} &\n\\mathcal{S} \\times \\mathcal{S}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{C}' \\cong\n(\\mathcal{C} \\times_{G_1, \\mathcal{S}, G_2} \\mathcal{C})\n\\times_{(p, q), \\mathcal{C} \\times \\mathcal{C}, \\Delta}\n\\mathcal{C}.\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-2}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ae6cf77909ac60b2bcdcfd765a02578083fbb954814cf633d6291e5e3015c9b1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f4971b79a70c6d269d97983013c857f38885ff7ea1a8a6dfa802ab4e6bffcf3", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a <MATH_0002>-fibre product of categories.\nThen there is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd21b47ff704fc487b1297a382fc4cfbae3d99bf655d3c328a8f6a7256c16dd4", "unit_id": "tag:003O:lemma-008"}
