ic statement, valid in any\n<MATH_0002>-category with <MATH_0003>-fibre products. Explicitly, it follows\nfrom the following chain of equivalences:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002>{X} <STRUCT_0003>_{(<STRUCT_0004>{X} <STRUCT_0005>_<STRUCT_0006>{Y} <STRUCT_0007>{X})}\n(<STRUCT_0008>{U} <STRUCT_0009>_<STRUCT_0010>{V} <STRUCT_0011>{U})\n& =\n<STRUCT_0012>{X} <STRUCT_0013>_{(<STRUCT_0014>{X} <STRUCT_0015>_<STRUCT_0016>{Y} <STRUCT_0017>{X})}\n((<STRUCT_0018>{X} <STRUCT_0019>_<STRUCT_0020>{Y} <STRUCT_0021>{V})\n<STRUCT_0022>_<STRUCT_0023>{V} (<STRUCT_0024>{X} <STRUCT_0025>_<STRUCT_0026>{Y} <STRUCT_0027>{V})) \\\\\n& =\n<STRUCT_0028>{X} <STRUCT_0029>_{(<STRUCT_0030>{X} <STRUCT_0031>_<STRUCT_0032>{Y} <STRUCT_0033>{X})}\n(<STRUCT_0034>{X} <STRUCT_0035>_<STRUCT_0036>{Y} <STRUCT_0037>{X}\n<STRUCT_0038>_<STRUCT_0039>{Y} <STRUCT_0040>{V}) \\\\\n& =\n<STRUCT_0041>{X} <STRUCT_0042>_<STRUCT_0043>{Y} <STRUCT_0044>{V} = <STRUCT_0045>{U}\n<STRUCT_0046>\nsee\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a1dd5504626f61ed9218cddfbe92043be827d34b69a59acfd584953e5c68970", "unit_id": "tag:003O:proof-p010"}
